      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, Maybe I didn\u0027t understand what you mean correctly, if this is the case, please give the implementation code. The following is my own understanding:\n\nThe usage of the const in the \"struct max17055_temp_profile\" is:\nstruct max17055_temp_profile {\n\tconst uint16_t t_gain;\n\tconst uint16_t t_offset;\n\tconst uint16_t t_curve;\n};\nconst struct max17055_temp_profile *temp_profile \u003d max17055_get_temp_profile();\n\nThe \"*temp_profile\" is a const, we cannot modify it\u0027s value except initialization. That is,the pointer \"temp_profile\" cannot pointer to another \"struct max17055_temp_profile\".\n\n\"const\" before \"uint16_t t_gain\" mean that we cannot modify it\u0027s value except initialization, which store the init value in ROM. Remove \"const\" before \"uint16_t t_gain\" mean that we can modify it\u0027s value any time, which store value in RAM.",
